  "reason": "The records collectively provide the relevant ingredients but not the later result. R6 establishes the exact AlCoCrFeNi2.1 FCC/B2 eutectic system, while R2 discusses interface coherency and deformation in a closely related Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloy. R3, R8, R10, and R17 show that intermediate-temperature aging or annealing can tune ordered phases and mechanical properties; R17 specifically supplies the closely related FCC/L12 structural motif. R4 links chemical ordering to inhibited screw-dislocation mobility and cross-slip locking, and R13 links ordering with plastic instability. However, none predicts that aging this exact eutectic alloy at about 600°C maximizes L12 order and jagged FCC/B2 boundaries to cause embrittlement, followed by ductility recovery near 750°C through diminished ordering and ductile boundary-transition zones. Reaching that specific non-monotonic intervention and coupled mechanism would require a substantial new insight."
